# Experiment Component Rules

Read `.agents/rules/experiments.md` for isolation rules and `.agents/rules/animations.md` for animation patterns.

## Size Discipline

| File Type | Target | Hard Limit |
|-----------|--------|------------|
| Orchestrator | ~120 lines | 200 |
| Section | ~60-90 lines | 150 |
| Data constants | ~100 lines | 150 |
| Hook | ~30-50 lines | 80 |

## Decomposition (trigger: >200 lines or 3+ visual sections)

```
ExperimentName.tsx     → thin orchestrator (lifecycle, shared state, composition)
data.ts                → all constants and configuration
sections/SectionN.tsx  → each visual section owns its own useGSAP scope
hooks/, shaders/       → extracted as needed
```

## Error reporting

- In error boundaries and route `error.tsx`, report to Sentry via `captureExperimentError` from `@/lib/sentry` when Sentry is enabled (env-gated).

## Animation Standards

- Always respect `prefers-reduced-motion` -- use `gsap.set` to reveal, never early return
- Vary motion vocabulary per section (clip-path, blur, scale, text split, parallax) -- don't repeat `opacity: 0, y: 40` everywhere
- Easing: ease-out for entrances, ease-in for exits. Never `linear` for UI.
- FOUC prevention: start hidden in CSS classes, not `gsap.set`

## Profile-Based Guidance

Check `experiment.json` for the `profile` field, then read `.agents/profiles/<profile>.md`:
- `scrollytelling` → Lenis + GSAP ScrollTrigger patterns
- `r3f-scene` / `r3f-shader` → R3F Canvas, useFrame, drei
- `interaction` → gestures, springs, drag
- `dom-effect` → CSS/shader effects on DOM
- `mixed` → scroll + 3D + interaction layer-cake composition
